WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.432
The checklist before a model enters your stack.

2
00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:06.445
On a team, put these in a pull request template for any new model.

3
00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:08.133
Repo and commit hash.

4
00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:12.232
License identifier and, for other, the license file reviewed.

5
00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:16.181
Base model, if it is a derivative, and the base model’s license.

6
00:00:16.461 --> 00:00:18.723
Gate status and who holds the access.

7
00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:26.192
Weight format (safetensors, or GGUF and MLX for local runtimes) and whether trust_remote_code is needed.

8
00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:30.717
The card’s intended use and any out-of-scope uses that touch your product.

9
00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:42.752
And the result of your own eval on a labeled sample, next to a frontier API on the same sample, because the card’s benchmark table is the publisher’s claim and your eval is your evidence.

10
00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:47.192
Lesson 3 adds the last line: whether it fits on the hardware you have.
